ID: vr-54
Title: Claire GLB and illustrated Blender robot workshop
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/53

Status: DONE
Milestone: Post-M1 local asset-authoring handoff
Dependencies: vr-08, vr-30, vr-53

Purpose:
  Export the existing Claire for the owner's Blender work and provide an
  editable Optimus-inspired armor study plus an image-heavy placement guide.
  The owner now dislikes the earlier procedural robot; historical approval
  does not establish approval of this or any later design.

Tasks:
  Verify pinned numerical Claire inputs and isolate a background Blender lane.
  Export named Claire skin/eyes/hair with matching PCA shape-key data.
  Build a separate editable helmet, optics, faceplate and mechanical-jaw study.
  Render actual orthographic, profile, exploded and annotated placement views.
  Deliver GLBs, native Blender source, illustrated PDF/HTML and provenance.
  Reimport exports into a fresh Blender process and verify their geometry/rig.
  Update chapters/index/ledger/tracking and preserve owned session context.

Acceptance criteria:
  Actual Blender-importable self-contained GLB; explicit scale/axes/origin.
  Claire preserves existing selected native vertices and matching PCA motion.
  Separate named editable armor pieces, not a reskinned copy of old robot.mjs.
  Guide prioritizes real model images with clear part labels and placement.
  Distinguish reference skin, static cosmetics, modal keys and mechanical rig.
  Never promise an automatic GLB roundtrip or speech/runtime integration.
  No live head/profile/device driven, new asset download or existing file overwrite.
  Keep model-derived binaries local/ignored with source and license notices.

